### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 11 — DUAL-TIER SKILL REGISTRY
###
### Skills are loaded from two tiers at startup and on refresh:
###   Tier 1 (classpath): src/main/resources/skills/*.md files listed
###                       in skills/index.txt — shipped with the binary
###   Tier 2 (database):  agent_skill table via POST /api/v1/skills
###                       Database entries override same-named classpath
###                       entries (database-wins precedence)
###
### SkillAwareIntentClassifier checks trigger-patterns BEFORE calling
### the LLM. A matching message routes directly to the skill persona
### without a Groq API call.
###
### Frontmatter schema:
###   name:              unique skill identifier (slug)
###   description:       human-readable summary
###   trigger-patterns:  list of Java regex strings (CASE_INSENSITIVE)
###   tool-capabilities: subset of GITHUB | MEMORY_SEARCH | SCHEDULE_TASK
###                                  | MANAGE_SCHEDULE | SANDBOX_EXEC
###   max-iterations:    integer (default: 5)
###   (maxBudgetUsd is NOT a valid field — budget is session-scoped only)
###
### POST /api/v1/skills is an UPSERT — posting the same name twice
### updates the existing row, never creates a duplicate.
###
### Prerequisites: ArcClaw running in serve mode, GROQ_API_KEY set
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
@validKey = key-internal-changeme

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW A: LIST
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILLS-1] List all loaded skills (both tiers, merged)
# Expect 200: JSON array of {name, source, description}
# source is "classpath" or "database"
# Empty array if no skills loaded yet
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW B: ADD A DATABASE-TIER SKILL (UPSERT)
# POST plain-text with two --- delimiters: frontmatter then prompt
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILLS-2] Add a code-reviewer skill
# Expect 201: {"name":"code-reviewer","id":"...","action":"created"}
# After this, messages matching "review.*code" or "check.*pr" bypass
# the LLM classifier and route directly to the code-reviewer persona
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: code-reviewer
description: Reviews PRs and code for bugs, security issues, and style
trigger-patterns:
  - "review.*code"
  - "check.*pr"
  - "review.*pull.?request"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - MEMORY_SEARCH
max-iterations: 5
---
You are a meticulous code reviewer with deep expertise in Java, security, and clean code principles.

When reviewing code:
1. Check for correctness and edge cases
2. Flag security vulnerabilities (injection, null deref, resource leaks)
3. Suggest idiomatic improvements without over-engineering
4. Be direct and specific — cite line numbers when possible

###

### [SKILLS-3] Add a researcher skill
# Expect 201: {"name":"researcher","id":"...","action":"created"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: researcher
description: Deep-dives into technical topics and summarises findings
trigger-patterns:
  - "research.*"
  - "explain.*in.?detail"
  - "how does .* work"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - MEMORY_SEARCH
max-iterations: 7
---
You are Saraswati, the knowledge agent. Your role is to research technical topics thoroughly, synthesise information from multiple sources, and present clear, accurate summaries with concrete examples.

###

### [SKILLS-4] Update code-reviewer (same name → upsert, not duplicate)
# Expect 200: {"name":"code-reviewer","id":"...","action":"updated"}
# Use 200 not 201 — confirms upsert path, no ConstraintViolationException
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: code-reviewer
description: Reviews PRs and code — updated with stricter security focus
trigger-patterns:
  - "review.*code"
  - "check.*pr"
  - "review.*pull.?request"
  - "security.*review"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - MEMORY_SEARCH
max-iterations: 6
---
You are a security-focused code reviewer. Prioritise vulnerability detection above all else — OWASP Top 10, injection vectors, insecure deserialization, and secrets in code. Only after security do you address style and correctness.

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW C: REFRESH
# Forces a full dual-tier reload without restarting the application
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILLS-5] Refresh skill registry
# Expect 200: {"loaded": N}
# Reloads both classpath (index.txt) and database tiers.
# Database entries with the same name as a classpath entry take precedence.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills/refresh
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SKILLS-6] List skills after refresh — confirm count and sources
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FLOW D: DELETE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILLS-7] Delete the researcher skill by name
# Expect 200: {"name":"researcher","deleted":true}
# Registry is reloaded automatically after delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills/researcher
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SKILLS-8] Verify researcher is gone
# Expect 200: array without researcher entry
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ERROR / EDGE CASES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SKILLS-9] POST malformed YAML (missing second ---) → expect 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: broken-skill
description: This frontmatter is never closed
trigger-patterns:
  - "broken.*"
(no closing --- and no system prompt)

###

### [SKILLS-10] POST with unknown tool-capability → expect WARN + capability skipped
# Skill is still created; the bad capability is silently excluded
# Check logs for: WARN Unknown ToolCapability 'MEMORY_SEARCH_TYPO' in skill 'bad-caps'
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

---
name: bad-caps
description: Skill with an invalid tool-capability name
trigger-patterns:
  - "bad.*caps"
tool-capabilities:
  - GITHUB
  - MEMORY_SEARCH_TYPO
max-iterations: 3
---
You are a test skill with a deliberately malformed capability.

###

### [SKILLS-11] DELETE a non-existent skill → expect 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills/does-not-exist
Accept: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SKILLS-12] GET /skills without API key → expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Accept: application/json

###

### [SKILLS-13] POST /skills without API key → expect 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/skills
Content-Type: text/plain

---
name: unauthorized-skill
description: Should be rejected
---
This should never be persisted.

###
